  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 192 of the laws of 2011, relating to authorizing\ncertain health care professionals licensed to practice in other jurisdictions\nto practice in this state in connection with an event sanctioned by New York\nRoad Runners, in relation to extending the provisions thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8206",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8206-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Chap 192 of 2011",
    "lawSection": "Public Health",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8206\n\nSPONSOR: SERRANO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 192 of the laws of 2011, relating to authorizing\ncertain health care professionals licensed to practice in other juris-\ndictions to practice in this state in connection with an event sanc-\ntioned by New York Road Runners, in relation to extending the provisions\nthereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo authorize certain licensed health care professionals from other\njurisdictions to practice in New York State with respect to certain\nmajor events sanctioned by New York Road Runners.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Provides the following list of events for which certain out\nof state healthcare professionals appointed by the New York Road Runners\nare authorized to provide professional services:\n\nEVENT                              DATE\n\nNew York City Half                 3.16.25\nBrooklyn Half                      5.17.25\nQueens 10k                         6.14.25\nBronx 10 mile                      9.14.25\nStaten Island Half                 10.12.25\nNew York City Marathon             11.2.25\n\nSection 2 of the bill would provide for the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew  York  Road  Runners events bring runners from all over the world to\nNYC. The efforts of healthcare workers at events like the  NYC  Marathon\nhelp  ensure that runners make it across the finish tine safely. Accord-\ningly, it would be advantageous to allow licensed  health  care  profes-\nsionals,  who are in good standing with their respective state or terri-\ntory, to provide services at these popular events.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nPrevious Authorization - S.9004 (Chapter 141 of 2024)\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately and shall expire and be deemed repealed December 31, 2025.\n",
